.TH SLCTL 1 "2026-10-18" "SparkLink" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slctl \- SparkLink device control utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slctl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slctl
is an interactive command\-line tool for controlling SparkLink wireless
devices. It communicates with the
.BR slkd (8)
daemon over D\-Bus.
.PP
When invoked without arguments,
.B slctl
enters an interactive shell with a
.B [slk]#
prompt. Command history is saved to
.IR ~/.slctl_history .
.SS Owned SSAP service
.B ssap-serve SERVICE_HEX PROPERTY_HEX OPS ACCESS VALUE_HEX [ask|allow|deny]
keeps one local service owned by its foreground D-Bus connection. Registration
is local staging, not remote publication success. The default ask policy prints
an original identity/deadline and accepts yes TOKEN or no TOKEN for that prompt;
local tokens are not reused within this process. value reads the same owner's
local value and quit unregisters. Owner exit revokes the registration.
Explicit allow/deny is local service policy, not security Agent approval,
authentication, encryption or Bond. Existing channel and Engine limits apply.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage and commands without connecting to D\-Bus.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the version without connecting to D\-Bus.
.TP
.B \-\-session
Use the session bus for isolated tests. The system bus is the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-adapter " path"
Select a live adapter registration for a one\-shot command. A command is required.
For example, use the path returned by
.B list
with
.B scan on
or
.BR "advertise on" .
.SH SUPPORT BOUNDARY
Unpublished controller-wide pair/security, legacy PHY/role/PM/AFH/ExtAdv,
privacy, sync, measurement and bare-handle service spellings are removed.
Current Connection security uses security-request and Agent.
Current SSAP operations
use the distinct ssap-* commands and canonical Connection objects. Consult
project/current-capabilities.md for exact source/artifact qualifications.
All experimental driver and real WS73 operations remain VM-only.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Discovery and Connection
.TP
.B list
List available adapters.
.TP
.B show
Show adapter information and status.
.TP
.B scan on|off
Start or stop device scanning.
.TP
.B peers
List typed peers under the selected controller generation. Advertisement validity,
unknown RSSI and unknown connection state are explicit. This grants no channel
or security authority.
.TP
.BI peer-observation " typed-peer-path"
Read the pinned daemon observation: raw vendor header/data, original Native
sequence and kernel boottime. RSSI is unknown for an unavailable or expired
observation or the SDK sentinel. This does not discover SSAP services or certify
physical connectivity. Old devices/info commands and address-only objects are removed.
.TP
.BI connect " address address-type"
Request an explicitly typed physical connection; controller management permission
is required. A Peer advertisement is not an authentication credential.
.TP
.BI disconnect " [address]"
Disconnect the current or specified device.
.SS Read-only Session Observation
.TP
.BI transport-status " connection-path"
Read the existing authorized Session transport snapshot through its current
SMTC owner. Does not start an Engine or open a channel. Missing owner returns
NotSupported; retirement, changed identity and the original one-second deadline
fail. Zero queues or debt do not prove callback drain, future idleness, firmware
completion accuracy or safe handle reuse. This unreleased API has no compatibility
promise; consult the exact artifact qualification.
.SS Explicit Reference Security
.TP
.BI agent " [method]"
Run one foreground, explicit human Agent for the selected controller. Method
is sdk111-no-mitm (default) or sdk111-numeric-comparison; no automatic approval.
Enter approve or reject followed by the exact current request id for initial
consent. Numeric comparison then requires confirm, request id and the exact
displayed six-digit code, or reject with that id. Compare with the intended peer.
Both callbacks share the original deadline; no renewal is allowed.
Quit, EOF and Ctrl-C unregister only this Agent, without stopping the controller.
A pollable terminal or pipe is required; input lines are limited to 512 bytes.
.TP
.BI security-request " connection-path [timeout-ms] [method]"
Allocate, begin and observe one author-owned request on the same bus connection.
Timeout is 1 through 5000 milliseconds, default 5000, including policy waiting;
approval never renews it. Start the passive T request before active G, with
explicit Agents on both controllers. Ctrl-C only attempts this request's cancel.
Both commands pin the original daemon owner and canonical connection identity.
These experimental commands require management/Agent permission, not just an
application channel grant. Exact CLI real-device qualifications are listed in project/current-capabilities.md;
they do not imply complete security or deployment support.
.PP
Success reports the selected limited SDK111 mechanism and observed installation.
The no-MITM method is unauthenticated. Numeric comparison needs separate local
confirmation and real peer proof; neither operation grants a trusted channel,
Bond or application delivery. The five-second budget includes both prompts;
general human pairing and numeric CLI physical qualification remain separate.
Rejection, timeout, ownership loss and incomplete native results exit nonzero.
Legacy Pair/Encrypt do not invoke this workflow.
.SS SSAP Services
The unpublished services, remote-services, read and write legacy commands
are removed. Use the distinct ssap-list/register/serve/remove/local-read
operations for local state and ssap-discover/read/write with an exact
Connection path for the implemented remote protocol. Local registration
is not proof of remote delivery; Owned authorization is separate from pairing.
.SS Statistics and Diagnostics
.TP
.B stats
Show the native LinkSnapshot summary; not mixed legacy subsystem counters.
.TP
.B events
Show the selected registration event position; not delivered/ACK/pending counts.
.SS Interactive Shell
.TP
.B help
Print the list of available commands.
.TP
.B quit\fR,\fP exit
Exit the interactive shell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
Override the system bus address for D\-Bus communication.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.slctl_history
Interactive shell command history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error communicating with slkd or invalid command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slktest (1),
.BR slkd (8),
.BR sparklink.conf (5)

.SH APPLICATION TESTS
Application correctness and performance exercises use slktest channel.
slctl manages devices, connections and authorization; it has no benchmark aliases.
